{
  "_comment": [
    "Synthetic Google Ads engine data for tools/harness.js. Lets you exercise",
    "slides 8-12 and the engine-only YoY fallback without deploying the MCC",
    "script or touching a real account.",
    "",
    "The shape of every tab here IS the contract engine-report.js must write.",
    "If you change a column name in one, change it in the other.",
    "",
    "In _eng_day, `_generate` expands to daily rows. Month offsets are relative",
    "to the month under test: 0 = report month, -1 = prior, -12 = year-ago.",
    "The -12 entry is the important one — the Triple Whale store does not reach",
    "back that far, so it exercises the path where %YoY engine columns are real",
    "while the Triple Whale columns must read n/a.",
    "",
    "{ \"scale\": N } is multiplied by the month's factor, so year-ago numbers",
    "come out proportionally smaller and the deltas are non-trivial.",
    "",
    "Campaign names deliberately mirror the real US account so the classifier is",
    "tested against naming it will actually meet, and the labels column exercises",
    "BRAND_LABEL_MAP taking precedence over the name regexes.",
    "",
    "Costs are CALIBRATED to the real July 2026 Google Ads spend in the Triple",
    "Whale export (~$219.7k) and land ~1.8% under it. That is deliberate: the",
    "self-test cross-checks engine cost against Triple Whale spend per channel,",
    "so a fixture inventing wildly different numbers would fail that check every",
    "run and train everyone to ignore it. A couple of percent is realistic drift;",
    "the check fires above 5%.",
    "",
    "_eng_bing carries MONTHLY-grain rows, exactly as the Microsoft Advertising",
    "Script POSTs them. Microsoft Scripts have no report query surface, so daily",
    "grain over two years would need ~790 sequential selector passes; monthly needs",
    "26. Dated the 1st with grain='month', which the Apps Script matches by MONTH",
    "and never by date range."
  ],
