  "_comment_product_dims": [
    "What each product dimension CONTAINS, written by fetchProductDims_() — one",
    "query per dimension, top 25 values each. Feeds Diagnostics → Show product",
    "dimensions, which is how you choose PRODUCT_DIM_1 / PRODUCT_DIM_2 instead of",
    "guessing and re-running the whole chain.",
    "",
    "Modelled on the real US feed as reported: custom label 1 is the single value",
    "'shoes' for every product, and custom label 4 is female/male/unisex. Both are",
    "therefore USELESS as a slide-8 category, which is the whole reason this tab",
    "exists — the diagnostic must rank them below product_type_l1 and say so.",
    "product_custom_attribute0 is mostly unpopulated, the other failure mode."
  ],
